{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd && sed -n '1,240p' AGENTS.md && if [ -f docs/AGENTS.md ]; then sed -n '1,260p' docs/AGENTS.md; fi && if [ -f RULES.md ]; then sed -n '1,260p' RULES.md; fi && gh issue view 45 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --comments\"","aggregated_output":"author:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nDependency check: #43 is closed, but #44 is still open. Per this issue’s explicit instruction not to start until both dependencies are closed, no implementation work has been started. I am leaving the status unchanged; this is dependency ordering, not a human/external blocker.\n--\nauthor:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nImplemented and pushed LALAL API v1 backend (commits 68ceb76, 28794f7). Includes v1 upload/split/check/limits/cancel/delete, durable source/task/idempotency checkpoints with fail-closed ambiguity handling, bounded polling and WAV download validation, effective-model pinning, mocked HTTP tests, and an opt-in manual smoke-test procedure. Verified: 55 backend/project tests and 19 analysis tests pass (3 pre-existing Python deprecation warnings).\n--\nauthor:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nFix cycle 1 complete: source-upload reuse is now durable and scoped by content hash, so the four original-source operations share one LALAL upload while the instrumental cascade uploads separately. Task/idempotency state remains operation-local. Added regression coverage; ============================= test session starts ==============================\nplatform darwin -- Python 3.11.15, pytest-9.1.1, pluggy-1.6.0\nrootdir: /Users/marekkucharski/projects/.pm-worktrees/vgt/issue-45\nconfigfile: pyproject.toml\nplugins: anyio-4.14.2\ncollected 27 items\n\ntests/test_lalal.py .....                                                [ 18%]\ntests/test_separation.py ......................                          [100%]\n\n============================== 27 passed in 0.64s ============================== passes (27 tests). Pushed commit b8b5d08.\n--\nauthor:\tmrkkucharski\nassociation:\towner\nedited:\tfalse\nstatus:\tnone\n--\nFix cycle 2 complete: preflight now uploads and prices authoritative source durations before any split, persists/reuses that source identity, and reserves the cascade. Expired task recovery creates and checkpoints a new idempotency identity only when required local output recovery is needed; downloads now validate task-reported duration against WAV metadata. Verified with `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lalal.py tests/test_separation.py` (31 passed).\n--\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/GOAL.md && git status --short --branch && git log --oneline -8 && gh issue view 45 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json title,body,labels,comments,url && gh issue view 43 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json state && gh issue view 44 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json state && rg -n \\\"Lalal|LALAL|idempotency|minutes_left|expired\\\" . --glob '\"'!uv.lock'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' docs/GOAL.md && git status --short --branch && git log --oneline -8 && gh issue view 45 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json title,body,labels,comments,url && gh issue view 43 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json state && gh issue view 44 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json state && rg -n \\\"Lalal|LALAL|idempotency|minutes_left|expired\\\" . --glob '\"'!uv.lock'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Implement the only network-touching piece: the LALAL.AI **API v1** backend behind the `Separator` seam. See **[docs/stem-separation-plan.md](../blob/main/docs/stem-separation-plan.md)** — sub-issue **B**, §1 (API v1), and Acceptance criteria (§5).\\n\\n**Depends on #43 (operation model + seam) and #44 (final paths).** Do not start until both are closed.\\n\\n## Scope — v1 endpoints\\n- Auth header `X-License-Key` from **`LALAL_LICENSE_KEY`**, never persisted or logged. (v0 `Authorization: license …` is deprecated — not used.)\\n- `POST /api/v1/upload/` → `POST /api/v1/split/stem_separator/` → poll `POST /api/v1/check/` (task_ids) → download; plus `/api/v1/limits/minutes_left/`, `/api/v1/cancel/`, `/api/v1/delete/`.\\n- **Do not** use `/api/v1/split/multistem/` — per-stem-minute billing gives no saving and one-task-many-outputs would break per-operation resume (see plan §1).\\n- Presets: `splitter` (default `auto`), `dereverb_enabled`, `extraction_level`, fixed `encoder_format=\\\"wav\\\"`. (There is **no** `enhanced_processing_enabled` in v1.)\\n\\n## Recipe (five paid operations, each reference stem from the ORIGINAL)\\nupload original → vocals [keep stem + instrumental] → bass/drums/guitar from original [keep stems] → upload instrumental → guitar [keep back = `backing`]. The final guitar op is the **only** cascade.\\n\\n## Must-have durability\\n- Generate + persist a UUID **`idempotency_key`** before submission; persist task id immediately on success; on restart resume a known task. Ambiguous submission whose task identity can't be recovered **fails closed** (no auto-retry, no second charge).\\n- Pre-flight `minutes_left` vs sum of outstanding operation durations (vocal pair counts once); a run that can't cover the outstanding recipe starts **no** new paid tasks.\\n- Poll < 30 req/min with bounded backoff; handle `429`, task errors, cancellation, upload/task expiry, expired download URLs; re-upload only expired sources.\\n- Stream downloads to `.part`, validate length + readable WAV metadata/plausible duration, atomic rename, store SHA-256/size/duration. Partial files never treated as cached. Record requested **and** effective presets (incl. the model `auto` chose; pin it on a reconstruction retry).\\n\\n## Tests\\n- Mock v1 HTTP fixtures in CI (**no live calls**); assert `X-License-Key` redacted from exceptions/progress/sidecars/snapshots. One explicitly manual, opt-in smoke test for an account owner before release.\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABK2DIWg\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Dependency check: #43 is closed, but #44 is still open. Per this issue’s explicit instruction not to start until both dependencies are closed, no implementation work has been started. I am leaving the status unchanged; this is dependency ordering, not a human/external blocker.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-20T13:22:36Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/45#issuecomment-5022730330\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOTcQqas8AAAABK2jhnQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"mrkkucharski\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"Implemented and pushed LALAL API v1 backend (commits 68ceb76, 28794f7). Includes v1 upload/split/check/limits/cancel/delete, durable source/task/idempotency checkpoints with fail-closed ambiguity handling, bounded polling and WAV download validatio