ackend is the authority on expiry\n./src/vgt/separation.py:595:    # LALAL's credit check is a run-level gate: it must happen before this\n./src/vgt/separation.py:628:        # LALAL preflight uploads the original solely to obtain its\n./src/vgt/separation.py:633:        # LALAL separation preserves timeline duration, and this conservative\n./docs/phase0-live-verification.md:39:# Repeat the exact select/apply/save sequence, then check it again for idempotency.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:6:Decisions from discussion: LALAL.AI (active subscription) is the default separator with Demucs as offline fallback; target machine is an M4 MacBook Air (16 GB, fanless); the primary workflow starts from a song already loaded in an **existing REAPER project**, so the importer augments the open project rather than generating a fresh one.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:20:**Non-goals for phase 1** (explicitly deferred): performance scoring, practice UI/looping logic (phase 2), tempo-ramped renders, tab generation (deprioritized in the source research as too error-prone to be the first investment), any hard cloud dependency — the default path uses LALAL.AI, but the tool must remain fully **offline-capable** via the Demucs fallback.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:34:│  vgt_analyze.lua                │             │  ingest → separate (LALAL/ │\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:62:| Separation | **LALAL.AI API** (default — active subscription; dedicated acoustic- and electric-guitar stems, which is the one stem that must be good; async upload → split → download, cached so each song costs credits once) | Demucs `htdemucs` 4-stem on MPS (offline fallback); `audio-separator`-style UVR/RoFormer backends later | Cloud upload in the default path (own files, personal use — fine, but noted); subscription lapse → fallback must always work; Demucs repo archived → pin version; skip `htdemucs_6s` guitar (experimental, bleeding — LALAL covers it) |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:120:Python 3.11 · `uv` for env/deps · `typer` CLI · `pydantic` manifest models · ffmpeg · LALAL.AI REST API (default separator) · torch (Demucs fallback; MPS) · ONNX Runtime (Basic Pitch) · Lua ReaScript with a vendored JSON decoder for the two REAPER actions.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:122:Target machine: **M4 MacBook Air, 16 GB unified memory** (confirmed). Two consequences: it's fanless, so sustained local separation would thermal-throttle — another reason LALAL-by-default is right; and with separation offloaded, the remaining local stages (madmom, chord CNN, Basic Pitch) are lightweight, putting expected end-to-end time at ~2–3 min/song plus upload. Fully offline operation (Demucs fallback) remains supported, just slower and warmer.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:129:| M1 | Separation stage: LALAL adapter (default) + Demucs fallback behind one `Separator` interface | guitar/bass/drums/vocals(/other) stems land in the song folder from either backend; stage cached so each song costs credits once | M |\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:143:- **Cloud in the default path**: LALAL API changes, credit exhaustion, or subscription lapse must degrade gracefully to Demucs — the fallback is exercised in tests, not just theoretical. Uploaded audio is the user's own, for personal practice.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:149:1. ~~Target machine?~~ Resolved: M4 MacBook Air, 16 GB. LALAL default; Demucs fallback on MPS.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:152:4. ~~LALAL.AI subscription?~~ Resolved: active — API adapter is the default separator, built in M1.\n./docs/phase1-song-prep-plan.md:156:On the target machine: open an existing REAPER project containing a song item → run `vgt: Analyze selected item` → pipeline completes (LALAL stems + local analysis) → `vgt: Apply results` augments the project per the tables above, non-destructively and idempotently; corrections in `corrections.yaml` survive re-runs; all analysis provenance is in `manifest.json`. Then phase 2 (practice controller: stem muting, loop/tempo management, take recording) builds on the same manifest and the same `[vgt]` track conventions.\n./docs/GOAL.md:83:Separate the reference track into practice stems using **LALAL.AI as the sole backend** — offline separation\n./docs/GOAL.md:86:deliberate cascade for the guitarless practice bed) and loading them as `[vgt]` tracks. The full design — LALAL\n./docs/GOAL.md:91:- **a LALAL v1 backend** behind a thin `Separator` seam, authenticated only by the `LALAL_LICENSE_KEY`\n./docs/GOAL.md:92:  environment variable (never persisted or logged), with idempotency-keyed, durably-checkpointed operations so\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:6:in the `llm-wiki` vault; the LALAL.AI REST API v1\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:16:**Scope decision (2026-07-20): LALAL.AI is the sole separation backend.**\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:23:manual LALAL workflow exactly — **no instrument probing, no configurable stem\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:53:- LALAL.AI is the cloud default; it exposes dedicated **acoustic-** and\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:55:  for a practice workflow. This is the decisive reason to build on LALAL.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:65:- Resilience caveat: LALAL is subscription-gated. With no offline fallback,\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:70:**From LALAL API v1:**\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:92:  idempotency/resume model below, where each paid stem is its own durably\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:95:- `POST /api/v1/limits/minutes_left/` reports remaining processing minutes.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:99:- Split requests accept a UUID idempotency key. It is a duplicate-charge guard,\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:108:(returning that stem and a back track), the recipe maps onto LALAL as:\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:116:  two retained artifacts but is billed once. `POST /api/v1/limits/minutes_left/`\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:123:- **Durable remote identity.** Each operation records its idempotency key,\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:128:  expired. Expiry of a completed remote task does not matter after validated\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:174:  HTTP/LALAL details while allowing a fake backend to exercise the same retry\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:175:  and resume logic. Only `LalalSeparator` is implemented now.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:176:- **Light dependency**: LALAL needs only an HTTP client (`httpx` or `requests`)\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:255:  backend_state, status, outputs, completed_at, error}`. LALAL backend state\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:256:  includes source id/expiry, idempotency key, and task id. Each artifact records\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:264:### B — LALAL API v1 backend (priority:high, L)\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:268:  from **`LALAL_LICENSE_KEY`** and is never persisted or logged.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:272:- Before any outstanding paid task, call `/api/v1/limits/minutes_left/` and\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:276:- Generate and persist a UUID idempotency key before submission; persist the\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:281:  cancellation, upload/task expiry, and expired download URLs. Re-upload only\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:282:  expired sources and never replace a completed operation merely because its\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:283:  remote record expired.\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:299:  checkpoint is atomically written immediately. If LALAL is unavailable, local\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:345:- On the golden songs, listen for interference/damage in the LALAL guitar and\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:356:- **Secrets**: `LALAL_LICENSE_KEY` is environment-only — documented in the\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:365:  (idempotency key + durably recorded task id + fail-closed on ambiguity) and\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:380:  a LALAL API change, credit exhaustion, or a lapsed subscription **blocks\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:405:- Missing key, exhausted credits, timeout, `429`, task error, expired source,\n./docs/stem-separation-plan.md:419:- A manual opt-in LALAL smoke test on one short owned audio file confirms the\n./tests/test_lalal.py:11:from vgt.lalal import AmbiguousSubmissionError, InsufficientMinutesError, LalalError, LalalSeparator\n./tests/test_lalal.py:46:            assert payload[\"idempotency_key\"]\n./tests/test_lalal.py:66:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler), sleep=lambda _: None)\n./tests/test_lalal.py:73:    assert checkpoints[1][\"idempotency_key\"] and \"task_id\" not in checkpoints[1]\n./tests/test_lalal.py:94:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler))\n./tests/test_lalal.py:113:        assert request.url.path == \"/api/v1/limits/minutes_left/\"\n./tests/test_lalal.py:114:        return httpx.Response(200, json={\"minutes_left\": 0})\n./tests/test_lalal.py:116:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler))\n./tests/test_lalal.py:130:        return httpx.Response(200, json={\"minutes_left\": 9.9})\n./tests/test_lalal.py:132:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler))\n./tests/test_lalal.py:135:    assert paths == [\"/api/v1/upload/\", \"/api/v1/limits/minutes_left/\"]\n./tests/test_lalal.py:138:def test_expired_task_reconstructs_with_a_new_durable_identity(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n./tests/test_lalal.py:161:    initial = {\"source_id\": \"source-1\", \"source_expires\": 4102444800, \"task_id\": \"expired\", \"idempotency_key\": \"old\"}\n./tests/test_lalal.py:163:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler), sleep=lambda _: None)\n./tests/test_lalal.py:167:    assert result.backend_state[\"expired_task_id\"] == \"expired\"\n./tests/test_lalal.py:169:    assert submitted[0][\"idempotency_key\"] != \"old\"\n./tests/test_lalal.py:170:    assert any(state.get(\"status\") == \"reconstructing\" and state.get(\"idempotency_key\") != \"old\" for state in checkpoints)\n./tests/test_lalal.py:188:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler))\n./tests/test_lalal.py:189:    with pytest.raises(LalalError, match=\"duration is implausible\"):\n./tests/test_lalal.py:202:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler))\n./tests/test_lalal.py:218:    separator = LalalSeparator(license_key=LICENSE_KEY, client=_client(handler))\n./tests/test_separation.py:75:            idempotency_key = (resume_state or {}).get(\"idempotency_key\") or \"fixed-idempotency-key\"\n./tests/test_separation.py:77:            checkpoint({\"idempotency_key\": idempotency_key, \"task_id\": task_id, \"status\": \"submitted\"})\n./tests/test_separation.py:83:    \"\"\"Small network-free model of LALAL's upload reuse behavior.\"\"\"\n./tests/test_separation.py:422:            checkpoint({\"idempotency_key\": \"k\", \"task_id\": \"t\", \"status\": \"submitted\"})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
